            <ArticleTitle>Fibrinopeptide-A as thrombotic risk marker in diabetic and atherosclerotic coronary vasculopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>93-100</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fibrinopeptide A was determined in 75 middle aged male patients, five control subjects and a control group of young medical students, divided into nine subsets. The FPA levels were significantly elevated in the patient group, particularly among the diabetics, when compared with the medical students and also age matched controls. Diabetic patients who smoked and had vascular pathology had high FPA levels even after they stopped smoking.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
